<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-section-deratapoint" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Derivative at a Point</title>

  <p> Compute the Derivative at a Point </p>

  <outcomes>
    <ul>
    <li>Graphically and algebraically explain the similarities and differences between the tangent line, secant line, slope of a tangent line, slope of a secant line, difference quotient and derivative.</li>
    <li>Explain why the definition of the derivative requires taking a limit and what the limit means in this setting.</li>
    <li>State the definition of derivative of a function y = f(x) at a specific point x = a (as a limit).</li>
    <li>Use the limit definition of the derivative to find the derivative of a function at a specified point, provided the limit exists. </li>
    <li>Find an equation in point-slope form for the line tangent to the graph of a differentiable function at a given point.</li></ul>
  </outcomes>
  

</section>